WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.063
Hi!
(audience loudly cheering)

2
00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:03.233
Thank you so much-
How you doing?

3
00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:04.910
For coming on the show.

4
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.140
We were so excited that you are here

5
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.679
and before we start, I have to ask what your message is

6
00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:14.069
to young girls like you who have a dream

7
00:00:14.069 --> 00:00:16.533
but don't know where to begin.

8
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.363
Follow your dreams,

9
00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:21.970 line:15%
Break those glass ceilings, be resilient,

10
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.433 line:15%
be strong, and you'll get there.

11
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.450
Oh, Chef RO, I mean, you really are the example.

12
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.256
So it's really amazing to ask life advice from you.

13
00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:35.920
Okay, will you take us through what we are making today?

14
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.060
The title is my favorite.

15
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.020
So this recipe is called Don't Be a Jerk

16
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.290
and it's basically a crab cake

17
00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.888
that I marinated in jerk marinade seasoning.

18
00:00:47.888 --> 00:00:51.870
And why is this dish meaningful to you?

19
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.970
So, I was raised by a single mother,

20
00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.160
I don't know my father,

21
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.600
but what I do know is that he's Jamaican.

22
00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.170
So I just really wanted to tap

23
00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.960
into the Caribbean side of myself.

24
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.729
I love it, okay, we're really excited

25
00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:06.800
to learn this meaningful, personal dish

26
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.680
from you that really is original.

27
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.210
So teach us, Chef RO, what's first?

28
00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.180
Yes, okay, so, easy,

29
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.620
I have my crab meat in the bowl, all right?

30
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.320
I have some lemon juice in there ready.

31
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.780
I'm gonna add my one egg to it.

32
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.569
The egg is gonna be kind of like a binder.

33
00:01:23.569 --> 00:01:27.101
I have my beautiful pre-made jerk marinade in here.

34
00:01:27.101 --> 00:01:30.770
This is gonna be the seasoning to our crab cake.

35
00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.990
It makes it extremely moist.

36
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.800
It makes it extremely spicy.

37
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.460
So we want to add all of that in there as well.

38
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.844
Of course, Ritz Crackers, Ritz Crackers are my favorite.

39
00:01:38.844 --> 00:01:41.210
So the Ritz give it some texture

40
00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.616
and it also gives a little bit of sweetness

41
00:01:42.616 --> 00:01:44.880
because that jerk is so spicy

42
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.350
because of that Scotch bonnet pepper.

43
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.420
So I got all of my Ritz in there

44
00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.520
and of course we're gonna season this

45
00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.960
with some salt, give it some love.

46
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.370
I finish it with some black pepper.

47
00:01:57.370 --> 00:01:59.040
And then we're gonna mix this all together, Drew.

48
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.192
So I have my gloves ready.

49
00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:03.133
If you want, if you have a rubber spatula,

50
00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.540
if you want to get in dirty with your hands,

51
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.990
it's all up to you.

52
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.300
I do have a rubber spatula, RO.

53
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.380
I actually just made it and it says,

54
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.542
Make Something Beautiful, Love, Drew.

55
00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:15.764
Oh, I like that, I like that.

56
00:02:15.764 --> 00:02:18.110 line:15%
So I'm just mixing this all together.

57
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.020 line:15%
I'm using jumbo lump crab.

58
00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.000 line:15%
So you don't really want it to be shreddy,

59
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.360 line:15%
but you just want to mix it together

60
00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.230
so everything holds together.

61
00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:29.220
So what I have here is my pre-made crab cakes.

62
00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.130
Okay, I used a ring mold,

63
00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.840
just because I wanted the crab cakes

64
00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.595
to be the same size as my Hawaiian toasted rolls.

65
00:02:35.595 --> 00:02:37.890
Once it's formed in the ring mold,

66
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.500
you're gonna take it and you're gonna put it

67
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.080
on that plate of panko.

68
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.210
And that's gonna be like the extra crispiness

69
00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.470
on the outside of our crab cake.

70
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.146
So I'm just gonna take this

71
00:02:48.146 --> 00:02:50.340 line:15%
and move it on-
Yup, so with your hands,

72
00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.130 line:15%
you wanna push out, yeah, you can do that.

73
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.960 line:15%
You can slide it right on there and then use your hands

74
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.870 line:15%
to push it out of the ring mold.

75
00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.930 line:15%
Exactly, and then slide it up, perfect.

76
00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.500
That's exactly what I did.

77
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.750
For the home cook to do such a professional

78
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.190
restaurant-level like move like a ring mold,

79
00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.950
it's really exciting.

80
00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.040
And then do I want to add the panko on top as well?

81
00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.500
Yes, so I put panko on top

82
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.530
and then I flip it over just to kind of press it down

83
00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.620
so that it has this nice coating.

84
00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.010
And then that's gonna stay in the refrigerator

85
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.731
for about 30 minutes minimum

86
00:03:24.731 --> 00:03:28.520 line:15%
or overnight, ideally, so that the egg binder,

87
00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.770 line:15%
the Ritz crackers, everything can just solidify together

88
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.340
so that you have a beautiful crab cake.

89
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.170
So we're gonna go right into our, I'm using corn oil.

90
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.280 line:15%
So you want to go until it's golden brown and delicious.

91
00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.600 line:15%
So about 30 seconds on each side.

92
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.430 line:15%
So, Drew, Drew,

93
00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.470
once you get golden brown and delicious,

94
00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.060
I just want to come and I want to blot this

95
00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.380
on a paper towel just to get that excess fat off, okay?

96
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.130
I'm gonna land right on the bottom

97
00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.943
of my Hawaiian toasted bread.

98
00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.930
So what we did was we made a jerk mayo,

99
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.230
because I like my sandwiches with mayo.

100
00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.760
I made the mayo from scratch.

101
00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.740
So I had my oil, my one egg yolk,

102
00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.560
and I added some of that jerk marinade

103
00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.620
that we made in the beginning for the crab cake

104
00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.640 line:15%
and I'm just gonna lightly put this on top of my bun.

105
00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:21.800 line:15%
And then a little tomato.

106
00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.600 line:15%
Would you like me to put-
With whatever you want-

107
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.400 line:15%
The crab cake first?
You can get creative here.

108
00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.233
Exactly.

109
00:04:26.233 --> 00:04:29.080
Chef RO, how would you like me to pile?

110
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.830
In what order, bread-

111
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.370
It's all up to you, Chef.

112
00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.160
This is where your creativity comes in.

113
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.510
You can use any kind, anything.

114
00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.520
You can use onion, you don't have to do onion.

115
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.610 line:15%
You can do whatever you would like.

116
00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.770 line:15%
You can do pickle, whatever you prefer.

117
00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.110 line:15%
So you make it how you would like to eat it.

118
00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:48.165
I'm gonna say that I really am piling on.

119
00:04:48.165 --> 00:04:51.520 line:15%
I like the accoutrement, I like onion

120
00:04:53.471 --> 00:04:56.623
and I like what feels like a restaurant burger.

121
00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.960
And I can't wait to try this crab cake.

122
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.460
Okay, here I go.

123
00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:03.410
You ready?

124
00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.770
You go for it first, let me know.

125
00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:06.603
Oh my gosh.

126
00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.680
This is incredible.

127
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.760
This is the best crab cake I've ever had in my life

128
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:13.948
and I'm a crab cake fan.

129
00:05:13.948 --> 00:05:15.710
Oh, thank you, Drew, thank you.

130
00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.010
I really appreciate that.

131
00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.720
I'm glad you liked this, Drew, thank you.

132
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.170
Chef RO, I'm so honored.

133
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.923
Do you think we can do this again?

134
00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.550
Listen, call, call me, I'm here.

135
00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.547
It's a date.

136
00:05:27.547 --> 00:05:29.008
It's a date, Drew, I'll see you soon.

137
00:05:29.008 --> 00:05:30.211
(Drew lightly shrieks)

138
00:05:30.211 --> 00:05:33.378
(bright upbeat music)

